This looks like a Caesar salad, with romaine lettuce coated in creamy dressing and possibly a few croutons or cheese. It sits on a square plate roughly 24 cm across, and the salad covers only a small part of it.

I estimate about 90 g of lettuce plus roughly 25 g of dressing, so about 100 g in total. Dressed romaine runs about 100-150 kcal per 100 g once the creamy dressing is counted. A typical Caesar dressing is about 150 kcal per 30 g, so 25 g adds roughly 120 kcal. The lettuce adds about 15 kcal, and a few croutons or some cheese might add 20 more. That gives roughly 150 kcal.

